  "summary": "The biblical pattern of judgment, displacement, longing, and eventual restoration that shapes Israel\u2019s memory and hope.",
  "historical_context": "Exile is the crisis of the northern kingdom and especially Judah, culminating in Jerusalem\u2019s fall and the people\u2019s deportation.",
  "ancient_near_east_context": "Imperial conquest and deportation were common in the ancient Near East, but Scripture interprets exile as covenant judgment and mercy.",
  "literary_context": "Exile appears in law, narrative, lament, prophecy, gospel, and apocalypse as both event and motif.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Exile shows that covenant disobedience has consequences, but also that God preserves hope through discipline and return.",
